  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of integrated lifesaving responses to populations affected by displacement and famine in South Kordofan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtThe proposed project in South Kordofan aims to enhance the food security status of affected communities in Dilling localities through the provision of agricultural inputs, training and livestock support. The project will directly benefit 41,150 individuals, including IDPs, refugees, and host communities. In Dilling, the most vulnerable households will receive critical agricultural inputs and necessary training services to enhance crop production. This includes the distribution of improved seeds such as sorghum and millet for household consumption throughout the year as well as groundnuts for market sale. On the field crop trainings will be conducted, comprising five sessions covering technical cultivation practices, seed propagation, and climate adaptation. Furthermore, vulnerable women heading households in these localities will receive goats&#xa0; along with necessary training and veterinary services. Animal husbandry training will be provided.&#xa0;These interventions are designed to improve food access and strengthen livelihoods, with a focus on climate-smart agriculture and training. Protection initiatives will provide essential services like mental health and psychosocial support (MHPSS), case management for vulnerable children, and support for survivors of sexual and gender-based violence (SGBV). Key activities include community-based protection monitoring, capacity building, and awareness raising to promote safer environments.To promote peace and social cohesion, the facilitation and strengthening of Peace Committee will be supported in Dilling locality. The committee will undergo training in conflict resolution and peacebuilding techniques, enabling them to address conflicts, particularly those arising between farmers and animal breeders. Furthermore, the committee will develop and implement a community-based action plan to improve social cohesion and address underlying grievances related to land access and market issues. ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
